MID_EV14_025_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_025_m01_001: Hello, Kalla. I understand you wanted to see me?
MID_EV14_025_m01_002: Oh, Leilidahna. So sorry to summon you like this.
MID_EV14_025_m01_003: It seems your first qualifier in the Heroic Games has\nbeen arranged at last.
MID_EV14_025_m01_004: Nice to meet you! I'm Anna. I help organize the\nHeroic Games.
MID_EV14_025_m01_005: Kalla told us right before the start of the games\nthat you wanted to participate.
MID_EV14_025_m01_006: It was...a bit out of the blue. And I'm not going to lie,\nit took a LOT of work.
MID_EV14_025_m01_007: Normally, the answer would have been just...no.\nBut a request from the goddess herself?
MID_EV14_025_m01_008: We worked it out, of course. But don't tell the other\nparticipants you received special treatment, please.
MID_EV14_025_m01_009: Now, here are the details about your qualifier.\nCould you look them over for me?
MID_EV14_025_m01_010: <TLP>Match: First Qualifier of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Rains of Palma\nLeader: Jasmine\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}　
MID_EV14_025_m01_011: Is it OK if I ask what our opponents are like?
MID_EV14_025_m01_012: Sure. From what I saw in the last qualifier, they like\nto use heavily armored foot soldiers.
MID_EV14_025_m01_013: Oh, that's great. I mean, if that's true, then we\nshould do OK against them.
MID_EV14_025_m01_014: Hmm...only if they don't have something unexpected\nup their sleeves.
MID_EV14_025_m01_015: Oh yes! There's one more important detail...
MID_EV14_025_m01_016: I need you to select your clan name right away.
MID_EV14_025_m01_017: That's short notice. I need more time...
MID_EV14_025_m01_018: Please, this one's easy! You see, Leilidahna and I\nhave both won the Rose of Caelus title.
MID_EV14_025_m01_019: And when the two of us fight side by side, we're like\na tempest of rose petals. Beautiful and powerful!
MID_EV14_025_m01_020: So, surely Rose Tempest is the perfect name for a\nclan with two gorgeous flowers like us!
MID_EV14_025_m01_021: I have to admit that's good. Besides, I'm quite fond\nof names with a touch of the wind in them.
MID_EV14_025_m01_022: Syracusio's windy opinions aside, I can't imagine you\nhave any objections, do you, Leda?
MID_EV14_025_m01_023: <NCA>Tell her that you like the name.
MID_EV14_025_m01_024: <NCB>Tell her you're uncertain about the name.
MID_EV14_025_m01_025: <ACA>Hmm, it's pretty good. Yeah, OK, I like it.
MID_EV14_025_m01_026: <ACB>It's pretentious, but I don't really care. Go with\nwhatever name you like.
MID_EV14_025_m01_027: Alright then, I'll go ahead and register your name!\nAnd with that settled, it's time I get going.
MID_EV14_025_m01_028: Best of luck with your match! I'll be rooting for you.\nI hope you'll excuse me now, Kalla.
MID_EV14_025_m01_029: She comes and goes like a fresh breeze. How very\npleasant, indeed.
MID_EV14_025_m01_030: Sirocco, you're not planning on seducing her...\nare you?
MID_EV14_025_m01_031: Hehe. Seduce a beautiful young woman like her?\nIt would be rather rude of me NOT to.
MID_EV14_025_m01_032: Really? My mother always told me that men who\nbehave like that are, um..."unprincipled."
MID_EV14_025_m01_033: Your mother is entirely correct, Mu. You would be\nwise to remember that.
MID_EV14_025_m01_034: Associate yourself with an unprincipled man...and\nyou could spend the rest of your life in his snare.
MID_EV14_025_m01_035: Oh, ah, that reminds me! I poked around town for\ninformation about the bandaged man we saw.
MID_EV14_025_m01_036: What did you find out? He certainly stands out in\na crowd, so someone must know something.
MID_EV14_025_m01_037: That's the thing—I came up with nothing. My guess\nis he doesn't wear the bandages around town.
MID_EV14_025_m01_038: It might be prudent to report this to the Divine\nSovereign so he can begin a formal investigation.
MID_EV14_025_m01_039: Hey, so, I don't know if this is related, but I heard\nthis strange rumor that's going around town.
MID_EV14_025_m01_040: With things the way they are, you never know what\nmight be related to what. Go on, Mu. Tell us.
MID_EV14_025_m01_041: Yeah, so apparently, some sort of ghost has been\nappearing in Dagsion at night.
MID_EV14_025_m01_042: A...a ghost? Do you mean one of the undead who\ncan sometimes be seen walking the streets?
MID_EV14_025_m01_043: No one knows who or what this ghost really is.\nPeople have just started calling it "the Phantom."
MID_EV14_025_m01_044: The...Phantom? What a very creepy story, Mu.
MID_EV14_025_m01_045: Hmm...is that so.
MID_EV14_026_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_026_m01_001: You've been slipping away in the middle of the night\nquite often of late.
MID_EV14_026_m01_002: If you don't mind my asking... Where are you going,\nand what are you doing?
MID_EV14_026_m01_003: I could ask the same of you. Shouldn't you be\nwarming some woman's bed at this hour?
MID_EV14_026_m01_004: Perfumed breezes are delightful, but even the wildest\nwinds must blow elsewhere sometimes.
MID_EV14_026_m01_005: On those occasions, I tend to find myself here at the\ntemple, alone.
MID_EV14_026_m01_006: But I see you've done your best to dodge\nmy question.
MID_EV14_026_m01_007: Do you really think I'm obligated to tell you how\nI like to spend my free time?
MID_EV14_026_m01_008: Perhaps not. But as your friend, I can't help but\nwonder...and worry.
MID_EV14_026_m01_009: "Friend"? You really think we're friends, do you?
MID_EV14_026_m01_010: You know very well that your vihuela is not an\nordinary instrument.
MID_EV14_026_m01_011: Obsidian is one of Drake's treasures. It corrupts the\nminds of those who play it. Without exception.
MID_EV14_026_m01_012: Your ancestor Cohen... He played it, and his tragic\nend is but one example.
MID_EV14_026_m01_013: It's true. I've felt this...corruption.
MID_EV14_026_m01_014: Sometimes, when I'm playing Obsidian, there's a\nvoice that echoes in my head...and it isn't my voice.
MID_EV14_026_m01_015: It issues commands. The first time I heard it,\nit said, "Strum your soul."
MID_EV14_026_m01_016: I've been hearing that voice more and more. It says\nthings like, "Destroy them, kill them, ruin them all."
MID_EV14_026_m01_017: There are times when I wonder if my desire\nfor revenge is even mine to begin with.
MID_EV14_026_m01_018: That's... Miss Leda, please, doesn't this\nworry you?
MID_EV14_026_m01_019: I've been doing some research on those who use\nDrake's treasures...
MID_EV14_026_m01_020: And hearing voices is a sign that the condition\nis quite advanced.
MID_EV14_026_m01_021: Is it? I don't know. It's not like this is new for me.
MID_EV14_026_m01_022: And it doesn't happen every time I play Obsidian.\nOnly when I'm...very upset.
MID_EV14_026_m01_023: This is just how it's been since the first time I picked\nup Obsidian.
MID_EV14_026_m01_024: That's quite a long time ago. I don't know what to\nmake of it.
MID_EV14_026_m01_025: Those possessed by one of Drake's treasures are\nsupposed to be difficult even to speak to.
MID_EV14_026_m01_026: But that's not the case with you. Perhaps there's\nsomething special about you?
MID_EV14_026_m01_027: Please. You're not telling me this because you're\nworried about my well-being.
MID_EV14_026_m01_028: If anything happened to me, it would upset Kalla.\nAnd all you care about is getting in her good graces.
MID_EV14_026_m01_029: As difficult as it may be for you to believe this, I am\nhonestly and sincerely worried for you.
MID_EV14_026_m01_030: This conversation is done. I don't have any more\ntime to waste here with you.
MID_EV14_026_m01_031: Understand this: revenge is the only thing I live\nfor now.
MID_EV14_026_m01_032: And only when I think about...him...does any color\nbleed into this stupid, gray world.
MID_EV14_026_m01_033: So, I won't let anyone—not even a so-called\nfriend—take that away from me.
MID_EV14_026_m01_034: Honestly...what sorrowful things you say.
MID_EV14_102_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_102_m01_001: I have a request, Leilidahna. Will you hear me out?
MID_EV14_102_m01_002: Of course, Kalla. I'm happy to do anything I can\nfor you.
MID_EV14_102_m01_003: Well, you see, I've been thinking how lovely it would\nbe to hear you play your vihuela again.
MID_EV14_102_m01_004: I'd love to play for you. But is that OK? Obsidian is...
MID_EV14_102_m01_005: Your vihuela has a grim history, that is true. But\nCohen...my child...played it for so many years.
MID_EV14_102_m01_006: I know it's a selfish request, but if I could hear it\nplayed again... Would you mind?
MID_EV14_102_m01_007: I am grateful to you, Leilidahna. It felt almost as if\nmy son were here with us.
MID_EV14_102_m01_008: When I look back on my time with Cohen, I feel\nas though I wasn't much of a mother to him.
MID_EV14_102_m01_009: I gave birth to him here at this very temple, you\nknow. He proved to be a gifted singer at a young age.
MID_EV14_102_m01_010: And as he grew, he dreamed of venturing out into\nthe world. He longed to explore, to write songs...
MID_EV14_102_m01_011: He wanted to meet new people, visit new places, and\nlet all the wonders he laid eyes upon inspire him.
MID_EV14_102_m01_012: My son vowed to return to the temple once he had\ncompleted a song that he was truly satisfied with.
MID_EV14_102_m01_013: And I thought this would be a good experience for\nhim. So...I gave him permission to leave the temple.
MID_EV14_102_m01_014: Before he left, Cohen told me that when the song\nwas complete, I would be the first to hear it.
MID_EV14_102_m01_015: But he never did complete the song...and he never\nreturned to me.
MID_EV14_102_m01_016: So, before Cohen was able to write his perfect song,\nhe...he...
MID_EV14_102_m01_017: My child never fulfilled his dream or his promise to\nme...but Leilidahna, his blood runs in your veins.
MID_EV14_102_m01_018: So, when you play for me here in this place, it brings\nme joy like nothing else can. I am truly happy.
MID_EV14_102_m01_019: If you don't mind me asking, what was Cohen's\nfather like?
MID_EV14_102_m01_020: He was a bad man, and I was so blinded by my\nlove for him I failed to see it.
MID_EV14_102_m01_021: He was silver-tongued and charming, and it was said\nhe spent each night with a different woman.
MID_EV14_102_m01_022: That awful man's sweet whispers wrapped around\nmy heart...and I gave him every favor in return.
MID_EV14_102_m01_023: But then I gave birth to Cohen, and after some time...\nhe disappeared.
MID_EV14_102_m01_024: Truly? That was the last time you saw him?
MID_EV14_102_m01_025: Truly. He has not shown his face to me since.
MID_EV14_102_m01_026: He sounds similar to someone else we both know.
MID_EV14_102_m01_027: Indeed he does. When I look at Syracusio...that\nrake...I can't help but be reminded of Cohen's father.
MID_EV14_102_m01_028: Honestly, why am I always surrounded by men\nlike that? *sigh* I wish I knew.
MID_EV14_102_m01_029: But Leilidahna, have you not fallen in love? You're so\nyoung. Surely there's someone you're interested in?
MID_EV14_102_m01_030: That's the last thing on my mind right now. Though...\nthere is a face I fantasize about night and day.
MID_EV14_102_m01_031: Bertrand's face—the face of my father's murderer.
MID_EV14_102_m01_032: Oh...
MID_EV14_102_m01_033: Heh. Sometimes I feel like I'm cursed.
MID_EV14_102_m01_034: There is one person only who occupies my every\nthought. It sounds like love, doesn't it?
MID_EV14_102_m01_035: I won't be free of this curse until I kill that man.
MID_EV14_102_m01_036: Love and hate—they're so similar, aren't they?\nBut once you're free, what will you do then?
MID_EV14_102_m01_037: I've never... That's not something I can think\nabout until it happens.
MID_EV14_102_m01_038: Oh, Leilidahna, what I want more than anything is\nfor you to forget this revenge and to find a happy life.
MID_EV14_102_m01_039: I'm...sorry. That's not something I can do. Not even\nfor you, Kalla.
MID_EV14_027_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_027_m01_001: Hello. You must be from the clans we'll be fighting\nbeside in the upcoming match.
MID_EV14_027_m01_002: Let me guess... The kitten here is Orchel, and the\nbride-to-be is Anatolia. Did I get that right?
MID_EV14_027_m01_003: Nice to meet you. I'm Leda. Look, I know we just\nmet, but I'm going to come right out and say it...
MID_EV14_027_m01_004: We all have the same goal: to win the match. So, let's\ntry to do right by each other while we're in there.
MID_EV14_027_m01_005: Agreed! We should work together, Leda.
MID_EV14_027_m01_006: I may be new to much of this, but I promise to\ndo my very best.
MID_EV14_027_m01_007: You know, kitten, you look a little strange...but you\nsound like a normal girl. Honestly, I'm relieved.
MID_EV14_027_m01_008: You're a priest, aren't you? That symbol makes me\nthink you're from...Credna's temple?
MID_EV14_027_m01_009: Yes, that's correct. I'm a lead priest at Credna's\ntemple. Heh.
MID_EV14_027_m01_010: Lead priest?! Wow, I'm surprised someone of your\nstation would take part in an event like this.
MID_EV14_027_m01_011: You seem familiar with temple life, Leda.
MID_EV14_027_m01_012: I suppose I am. I was sent to live at Kalla's temple\nfor several years when I was a child.
MID_EV14_027_m01_013: Oh my, yes, that makes sense! I thought you had a\nparticular air about you.
MID_EV14_027_m01_014: If you don't mind my saying, you move with such\nprecision. Not much gets past your guard, does it?
MID_EV14_027_m01_015: Those aren't the kind of skills someone learns\novernight.
MID_EV14_027_m01_016: Hmm, I wonder if you're as young as you seem.\nHow long have you been working for the temple?
MID_EV14_027_m01_017: It's been 18 years...plus perhaps about two\nhundred more.
MID_EV14_027_m01_018: That's incredible! I suppose you aren't exactly a\nkitten after all.
MID_EV14_027_m01_019: {SetColor=Gray}She could be a demigod or something. There must be\na reason she's hiding her face.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_027_m01_020: {SetColor=Gray}Whatever's going on with her, I bet it explains why\nshe seems so...sheltered.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_027_m01_021: You all don't look like most of the folks from around\nhere either. Where do you call home?
MID_EV14_027_m01_022: Call home? Oh, you're curious where we're from?\nWe came from the village of Kun—
MID_EV14_027_m01_023: Er, um! We're from the...western part of the Nysiades\nregion, as a matter of fact!
MID_EV14_027_m01_042: Er, um! We're from the...western part of the Nysiades\nregion, as a matter of fact!
MID_EV14_027_m01_024: Yes, it's near the wall of the forbidden land. We grew\nup within sight of the Fezzan Gate.
MID_EV14_027_m01_025: So we're not overly familiar with cities like this one.\nI'm sure we appear out of place.
MID_EV14_027_m01_026: Hmm. So...you're from the desert? I guess that's why\nyour clothes look so...unusual.
MID_EV14_027_m01_027: {SetColor=Gray}She didn't seem to notice, so maybe we're clear...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_027_m01_028: {SetColor=Gray}If anyone found out you're of the White Egg, we'd be\nin a world of trouble right now.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_027_m01_043: {SetColor=Gray}She didn't seem to notice, so maybe we're clear...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_027_m01_044: {SetColor=Gray}If anyone found out you're of the White Egg, we'd be\nin a world of trouble right now.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_027_m01_029: Everyone's calling you the "Mystery Bride."
MID_EV14_027_m01_030: I can see why—your outfit is stunning. Is that what\nbrides wear where you're from?
MID_EV14_027_m01_031: Come on. You can tell me—did you really come to\nDagsion to find yourself a groom?
MID_EV14_027_m01_032: No, this is Mediator attire. It's designed for\nfunctionality.
MID_EV14_027_m01_033: It defends against dust, sunlight—even magic. My\nclothing is also designed for ease of movement.
MID_EV14_027_m01_034: So no, I am no one's "bride." Nor am I seeking\na groom.
MID_EV14_027_m01_035: {SetColor=Gray}Hmm, she's peculiar as well. I suppose that's fine.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_027_m01_036: That said, while I am not seeking a groom, I am in\nsearch of someone else. My prince.
MID_EV14_027_m01_037: Hmm. That's nice. I wish you the best in your\nsearch for him.
MID_EV14_027_m01_038: Thank you, Leda.
MID_EV14_027_m01_039: I'm sure you all feel the same, but the only thing\nI care about is winning this.
MID_EV14_027_m01_040: We might be enemies in the future, but right now\nwe're allies. So let's work together!
MID_EV14_027_m01_041: Looks like I'm going to have to do my best if I don't\nwant this strange crew to outshine me.
MID_EV14_028_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_028_m01_001: The year is 551 by the Dagdan Calendar. The place\nis the land of Fezzan. The battle...one for the ages!
MID_EV14_028_m01_053: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_054: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_055: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_002: It was there in the Chronos Desert, in a sea of\nscorching sand too cruel to sustain any living thing...
MID_EV14_028_m01_003: A giant egg the size of a mountain loomed over the\nland! It slept and it slept, until one day...it awoke!
MID_EV14_028_m01_004: On that foul day, cursed ones crawled forth, bringing\nwith them a terrible calamity!
MID_EV14_028_m01_005: It was Dagda the Great who gathered a force to stop\nthem, launching his grand conquest.
MID_EV14_028_m01_006: Thus began the land of Dagda's battle for survival...\nand the Battle of Fezzan!
MID_EV14_028_m01_007: To the east, the famed mercenary crew—Rains of\nPalma—representing the Dagdan Imperial Army.
MID_EV14_028_m01_008: To the west, representing the People of the White\nEgg, a lovely alliance of ladies from across the world!
MID_EV14_028_m01_009: Quiver with anticipation, onlookers, for our epic\nbattle is about to begin!
MID_EV14_028_m01_010: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_011: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_012: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_013: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_014: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_015: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_016: Wow! Sand! I can't believe it. The arena's\na...a desert!
MID_EV14_028_m01_017: Hrm... Truly incredible. They've built a desert\nenvironment...and with such accuracy.
MID_EV14_028_m01_018: They have always had the ability to change the\nappearance of the colosseum to fit a theme...
MID_EV14_028_m01_019: Still, this is very elaborate. The Heroic Games have\nput a talented playwright to work, it seems.
MID_EV14_028_m01_020: But...but...with the arena done up like this, we're\ngoing to get sand in our hair and all over our clothes!
MID_EV14_028_m01_021: You'd get covered in dust and sand in a normal\narena too, you know.
MID_EV14_028_m01_022: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_023: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_024: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_025: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_026: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_027: 
MID_EV14_028_m01_028: I've been told the western bards love to sing about\nthe Battle of Fezzan.
MID_EV14_028_m01_029: Most of their songs praise the empire's victory. But if\nyou look at it from the other side...it's a tragedy.
MID_EV14_028_m01_030: I get the sense that it'd be challenging to find\nsomeone here who'd consider both sides...
MID_EV14_028_m01_031: Hmm. An army invaded my hometown when I was\njust a child.
MID_EV14_028_m01_032: So, perhaps I tend to empathize with whatever side\nis getting trampled under boots.
MID_EV14_028_m01_033: Speaking of which, aren't you from Fezzan?
MID_EV14_028_m01_034: Yes. Though we don't hold special feelings for\nthe place.
MID_EV14_028_m01_035: Ultimately, it's nothing more than lines on a map,\ndrawn in by the empire.
MID_EV14_028_m01_036: Uh... If you say so. Well, it's time to show them\nwhat we can do.
MID_EV14_028_m01_037: There may be people who think like her, but we're\nstill painted as the villains in this country...
MID_EV14_028_m01_038: I knew to expect this, but I still feel raw about it. Our\npeople never harbored ill will toward anyone...
MID_EV14_028_m01_039: Just remember that this is nothing more than a\nplay—an impression of how the empire sees it.
MID_EV14_028_m01_040: Our focus must remain now on the future rather than\ntheir interpretation of the past. We must win this.
MID_EV14_028_m01_041: You're right. All that matters is winning right now.
MID_EV14_028_m01_042: Huh. So the opposing team this time is a flock of\nbeautiful women.
MID_EV14_028_m01_043: Though who knows what's happening under that\ngirl's mask.
MID_EV14_028_m01_044: She's got to mean you, Orchel.
MID_EV14_028_m01_045: Oh my, I know it's strange. But I must never\nremove this mask.
MID_EV14_028_m01_046: Sorry to ask, but please, don't pay it any\nattention.
MID_EV14_028_m01_047: Huh... Fine by me. I'm sure you've got your reasons\nfor wearing it.
MID_EV14_028_m01_048: But seriously—you're all just so beautiful, like\nprecious jewels or something. You're...dazzling.
MID_EV14_028_m01_049: The heavens clearly shined down upon you all\nwhen you came into this world.
MID_EV14_028_m01_050: And you have a presence. Not like any old fighters.\nFeels powerful...like a blast of storm wind.
MID_EV14_028_m01_051: Compared to this group, we must seem like\na bunch of boring weeds.
MID_EV14_028_m01_052: But you know what? Today we're going to show\neveryone just how stubborn a bunch of weeds can be.
MID_EV14_029_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_029_m01_001: Well, that was a crushing defeat. But I'm proud that\nwe got this far.
MID_EV14_029_m01_002: I'm sorry. I didn't mean to dash your dreams so\nthoroughly there.
MID_EV14_029_m01_003: I'd be lying if I said I wasn't frustrated, but losing\nis just part of the deal.
MID_EV14_029_m01_004: Besides, it's the losses that make you really\nappreciate the wins, right?
MID_EV14_029_m01_005: It was a close call for us too, you know. We were\npretty evenly matched.
MID_EV14_029_m01_006: I could sense your conviction. That must be where\nyou draw strength from.
MID_EV14_029_m01_007: That's nice of you to say. If you have a minute, I'll\ntell you a little story.
MID_EV14_029_m01_008: See, the name Rains of Palma is the name of the\nmercenary band that my husband and I started.
MID_EV14_029_m01_009: Our crew went through a lot together, and my\nhusband... He died a while back.
MID_EV14_029_m01_010: But the group we built together—and that he left\nbehind—they're my family.
MID_EV14_029_m01_011: It wasn't easy to keep us together after he died.\nMoney was tight, and we had to disband for a while.
MID_EV14_029_m01_012: We all went our separate ways to find work, hoping\nto pull in enough cash to get back together.
MID_EV14_029_m01_013: If we're going to rebuild our crew, we gotta fill our\ncoffers. So that's why I entered the Heroic Games.
MID_EV14_029_m01_014: We had a great match today, and I have no regrets.\nWhy? Because I got our crew's name out there.
MID_EV14_029_m01_015: If you can believe it, we're already getting asked\nabout new contracts. So things are good.
MID_EV14_029_m01_016: The crew's scattered all over the place, but if we\nkeep this up, we'll be back in business soon enough.
MID_EV14_029_m01_017: So, your dream does not die here. It lives and it\ngrows...
MID_EV14_029_m01_018: That is very admirable, Jasmine. And what more can\nwe ask of a dream but for it to live on?
MID_EV14_029_m01_019: I will pray for you and your self-made family to come\ntogether once again.
MID_EV14_029_m01_020: You're a strange girl, you know that? But I hope you\nget to follow your dreams too—wherever they lead.
MID_EV14_029_m01_021: And seeing how you pounded us into the sand,\nI hope you keep on winning!
MID_EV14_029_m01_022: If you don't, our reputation will take a hit. So, keep\nit up, would ya?
MID_EV14_029_m01_023: OK, we will do our best. Take care of yourself,\nJasmine.
MID_EV14_029_m01_024: Gracious, even in defeat. She is very pleasant.
MID_EV14_029_m01_025: Indeed she is. That is no weed. She is just a very\nhearty flower, to be sure.
MID_EV14_029_m01_026: She reminds me of my mother.
MID_EV14_029_m01_027: Fighting for her family is the most important thing\nto her. I think that's what my mom is doing too.
MID_EV14_029_m01_028: Family is important. I'd like to see House Cohendia\nrestored as well...for the sake of Lord Guillermo.
MID_EV14_029_m01_029: 
MID_EV14_029_m01_030: 
MID_EV14_029_m01_031: 
MID_EV14_029_m01_032: 
